  "title": "Context Assembly as the Controlled Variable",
  "summary": "This paper presents a control-theoretic approach to frozen LLM agents, where context assembly is treated as the controlled variable, learned online by a contextual bandit or REINFORCE policy. It evaluates a control system that optimizes execution state and data records, while improving accuracy and cost efficiency through set-valued prediction. The paper provides a formal decomposition and stability/uncertainty evidence for a control-theoretic claim.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The paper introduces a formal decomposition of the control system into inner and outer policies.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It demonstrates stability for the online controller in the sense used by Zhang et al. (2026).",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The paper evaluates the control system across three domains and two model providers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
